    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Riders With A Passenger Traffic Preparation</h1>
    <p>Hanoi traffic is a flow rather than a set of rules, and riding two-up inside that flow is a skill the pair learns together in the first hour and refines for the rest of the rental. Preparation is the right word, because very little of two-up city riding is difficult and almost all of it is easier with expectations set in advance: what the lanes are really for, how junctions read, where the machine feels its extra mass, and when the honest answer is a pause and a coffee rather than one more junction in the rain.</p>
    <p>This page is the traffic chapter of the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster for riders with a passenger. The verified fleet prices are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, general questions are on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the two chapters that feed into this one are the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/riders-with-a-passenger-bike-choice/">bike-choice page</a> and the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/riders-with-a-passenger-pre-ride-inspection/">pre-ride inspection routine</a>.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Why two-up traffic reading is different</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">The first hour: route choice and lane habits</a></li>
